# Test: the looking glass shows what a refused request said
# VALIDATES: AC-5 -- a 4xx carrying an error fragment reaches the operator in
#            the looking glass, inside the panel the request targeted
# PREVENTS: an interface nobody exercised. htmx 2 swapped no 4xx, so lg's error
#           fragments have never run in a browser. lg needs no error-event
#           handler for this: every request it issues names a content panel, so
#           htmx 4 lands the fragment where the operator was looking. The proof
#           is that it lands INSIDE #results and not over the form.
#
# The refusal is real and an operator can produce it by pasting a long filter.
# maxFormBytes (internal/component/lg/handler_ui.go) caps a search body at 4096
# bytes and handleUISearch answers a larger one with 400 "invalid form data".
# Every other lg validation failure answers 200 with a rendered banner, so this
# is the one 4xx the looking glass UI can reach.

option=server:kind=lg-no-engine
option=timeout:value=60s

action=open:path=/lg/search
expect=element:id=results

# POSITIVE CONTROL. A search the handler accepts posts and swaps #results, so a
# red below is about the refusal rather than about a form that never sent. The
# engine is down in this server, and saying so is a 200 answer.
#
# Enter submits, rather than a click on the Search button: the page carries the
# word Search three times (the heading, the tab, the button) and the runner
# clicks the first element whose snapshot line contains the text.
action=fill:id=prefix:value=10.0.0.0/24
action=press:id=prefix:key=Enter
action=wait:ms=1500
expect=html:contains=<div id="results"><div class="error-banner">

# PRE-CONDITION. No fragment on the page yet.
expect=html:not-contains=error-fragment

# 4200 bytes of AS path. ParseForm refuses the body before any engine query.
action=fill:id=aspath:
action=press:id=aspath:key=Enter
action=wait:ms=1500

# The fragment landed inside the panel the form targeted, with the message the
# handler wrote. The nesting is the assertion: a fragment htmx swapped over the
# form would carry the same words and leave the operator no way to search again.
expect=html:contains=<div id="results"><div class="error-fragment"
expect=html:contains=invalid form data
